{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequence.ts#L76","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHotkeySequence.ts:76"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue composable for registering a keyboard shortcut sequence (Vim-style)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This composable allows you to register multi-key sequences like 'g g' or 'd d'\nthat trigger when the full sequence is pressed within a timeout."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Shift+R"},{"type":"text","value":" then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Shift+T"},{"type":"text","value":"). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sequence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sequence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MaybeRefOrGetter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequence"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array of hotkey strings that form the sequence"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"callback","children":[{"type":"text","value":"callback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyCallback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function to call when the sequence is completed"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MaybeRefOrGetter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseHotkeySequenceOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"> = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options for the sequence behavior"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { useHotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\n// 'g g' to go to top\nuseHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => {\n  scrollToTop()\n})\n\n// 'd d' to delete line\nuseHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => {\n  deleteLine()\n})\n\n// 'd i w' to delete inner word\nuseHotkeySequence(['D', 'I', 'W'], () => {\n  deleteInnerWord()\n}, { timeout: 500 })\n\n// Same modifier on consecutive steps (bare Shift between chords is ignored)\nuseHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => {\n  nextAction()\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>...</div>\n</template>","lang":"vue"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"sequence","text":"sequence","level":3},{"id":"callback","text":"callback","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeySequence.ts:76](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequence.ts#L76)\n\nVue composable for registering a keyboard shortcut sequence (Vim-style).\n\nThis composable allows you to register multi-key sequences like 'g g' or 'd d'\nthat trigger when the full sequence is pressed within a timeout.\n\nEach step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. `Shift+R` then `Shift+T`). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### sequence\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<`HotkeySequence`\\>\n\nArray of hotkey strings that form the sequence\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\nFunction to call when the sequence is completed\n\n### options?\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md)\\> = `{}`\n\nOptions for the sequence behavior\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useHotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\n// 'g g' to go to top\nuseHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => {\n  scrollToTop()\n})\n\n// 'd d' to delete line\nuseHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => {\n  deleteLine()\n})\n\n// 'd i w' to delete inner word\nuseHotkeySequence(['D', 'I', 'W'], () => {\n  deleteInnerWord()\n}, { timeout: 500 })\n\n// Same modifier on consecutive steps (bare Shift between chords is ignored)\nuseHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => {\n  nextAction()\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>...</div>\n</template>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useHotkeySequence\ntitle: useHotkeySequence\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeySequence.ts:76](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequence.ts#L76)\n\nVue composable for registering a keyboard shortcut sequence (Vim-style).\n\nThis composable allows you to register multi-key sequences like 'g g' or 'd d'\nthat trigger when the full sequence is pressed within a timeout.\n\nEach step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. `Shift+R` then `Shift+T`). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### sequence\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<`HotkeySequence`\\>\n\nArray of hotkey strings that form the sequence\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\nFunction to call when the sequence is completed\n\n### options?\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md)\\> = `{}`\n\nOptions for the sequence behavior\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useHotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\n// 'g g' to go to top\nuseHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => {\n  scrollToTop()\n})\n\n// 'd d' to delete line\nuseHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => {\n  deleteLine()\n})\n\n// 'd i w' to delete inner word\nuseHotkeySequence(['D', 'I', 'W'], () => {\n  deleteInnerWord()\n}, { timeout: 500 })\n\n// Same modifier on consecutive steps (bare Shift between chords is ignored)\nuseHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => {\n  nextAction()\n})\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>...</div>\n</template>\n```\n"}
